Group H of the [[2014 FIFA World Cup]] consisted of [[Belgium national football team|Belgium]], [[Algeria national football team|Algeria]], [[Russia national football team|Russia]] and [[South Korea national football team|South Korea]]. Play began on 17 June and ended on 26 June 2014. The top two teams, Belgium and Algeria, advanced to the round of 16.

